meta {
  name: WS - Navigate Slides
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

# WebSocket commands — use a WS client.
# Connect to: ws://{{host}}/ws?token={{authToken}}
# A screen that draws SVG slides from presenter.frame adds &presenter=frames to get
# presenter.state without the SVGs (svgOmitted: true).
# All navigation commands broadcast presenter.slide_changed to all clients.

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/ws
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  ## WS: slide navigation commands

  All commands broadcast `presenter.slide_changed` to every connected client.

  | Command | Extra fields | Description |
  |---|---|---|
  | `presenter.next`  | —            | Advance one slide |
  | `presenter.prev`  | —            | Go back one slide |
  | `presenter.first` | —            | Jump to slide 1 |
  | `presenter.last`  | —            | Jump to last slide |
  | `presenter.goto`  | `slide: N`   | Jump to slide N |
  | `presenter.unload`| —            | Clear the presentation |
  | `presenter.status`| optional `svg: true` | Reply to sender with `presenter.state`; `svg: true` includes the SVGs for a `presenter=frames` client |
  | `presenter.frame` | `slide: N, width: W, height: H` | Reply to sender with one binary message: SVG slide N as a W×H JPEG (up to 3840×2160) |

  **Broadcast response for next/prev/first/last/goto:**
  ```json
  { "type": "presenter.slide_changed", "currentSlide": 3, "totalSlides": 12 }
  ```

  **Response for unload / load (sent to all clients):**
  ```json
  { "type": "presenter.state", "state": { "loaded": false, ... }, "svgOmitted": false }
  ```

  **Screens that draw slides from `presenter.frame`** connect with
  `ws://{{host}}/ws?presenter=frames`. Their `presenter.state` messages carry
  `"svgOmitted": true` and an empty `svg` in every `svgSlides` entry, which keeps a deck
  with photos from being sent to them in full on every change. To draw a slide itself,
  such a screen asks once with `{ "type": "presenter.status", "svg": true }`.

  A client that is slow to receive gets only the newest `presenter.state`: one still
  queued for it when a newer one is broadcast is dropped, with the slide changes that
  moved within it.

  **Example — jump to slide 5:**
  ```json
  { "type": "presenter.goto", "slide": 5 }
  ```
}
